{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A sorceress shall not live.</b> It is juxtaposed to 'if he entices,' because those who desire — their thought being evil — will seek ways of sorcery to fulfill their desire." "<b>Shall not live.</b> As its translation: לא תחי. And the translator who rendered לא תיחי errs, since we do not read לא תחיה but rather לא תחיה. Its death penalty is left unspecified, to teach you that whoever gets to her first is privileged, for if you delay her until she stands in judgment she will perform sorcery to escape."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:47.842252930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}